abstract: >-
  Course website and syllabus for "Introduction to Digital Humanities", an annual course taught
  in the autumn semester at the University of Bern (Walter Benjamin Kolleg / Digital
  Humanities). The course is compulsory for students of the MA Major and MA Minor in Digital
  Humanities and open to students from other humanities programmes. Over fourteen sessions it
  follows the chain from source to published data: definitions of the field, data and metadata,
  conceptual data modelling, Linked Open Data, data publication on the web, scholarly digital
  editions, and the analysis of networks, text corpora and geodata, closing with machine
  learning, large language models, data feminism and the FAIR and CARE principles. The course
  runs in parallel with the hands-on DH Lab.
